  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nSkies will clear and winds will ease tonight with high pressure\nmoving overhead. The clear skies and light winds will allow for\nefficient radiational cooling and the first hard freeze of this\nseason is expected for the entire region. The only active\ngrowing season counties are Luzerne and Lackawanna, so a Freeze\nWarning is in effect for them through tomorrow morning. \n\nLow temperatures will be in the 20s across the region. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nHigh pressure will stay over the region through the week and\ninto next weekend. A coastal low will develop well of the North\nCarolina Coast tomorrow and remain off the coast through most \nof the work week. This system is expected to pose no impacts at\nall for our area and models have trended the track further out\nto sea, with high pressure stiff arming precipitation \nassociated with the low and keeps it off the coast. Gradual \nwarm air advection after tonight will help temperatures get back\nto or even a little above seasonable normals by Monday. \nTemperatures will vary little after Sunday with highs \nconsistently in the 60s and lows in the 30s and 40s. Some valley\nlocations will approach the 70s for daytime highs during the \nmidweek period.\n\nAlso, this pattern is perfect for river valley fog to develop\neach night.",
